# eslint-snapshot-rule-tester format: v1


Test: no-invalid-init-directive >> invalid >>> docs/rules/no-invalid-init-directive.md incorrect 1
Filename: no-invalid-init-directive-incorrect-1.mmd

Code:
  1 | %%{init: {"theme": "dark",}}%%
    | ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  2 | flowchart LR
  3 |   A --> B
  4 |

Output:
  1 | %%{init: {"theme": "dark"}}%%
  2 | flowchart LR
  3 |   A --> B
  4 |

[1] mermaid.js reads no settings from this init directive because its JSON argument is invalid.
---


Test: no-invalid-init-directive >> invalid >>> docs/rules/no-invalid-init-directive.md incorrect 2
Filename: no-invalid-init-directive-incorrect-2.mmd

Code:
  1 | %%{INIT: {"theme": "dark"}}%%
    | ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ [1]
  2 | flowchart LR
  3 |   A --> B
  4 |

Output:
  1 | %%{init: {"theme": "dark"}}%%
  2 | flowchart LR
  3 |   A --> B
  4 |

[1] mermaid.js reads no settings from `INIT`; init directive names are case-sensitive.
---


